**Training Tip for Your Team:**  
When reviewing messages, look for patterns rather than isolated words. Abuse typically includes threats, discriminatory remarks, sustained personal attacks, or language intended to intimidate or harass. If a message crosses into any of these categories, your team should document it, avoid engaging with the hostile language, and follow Northwind Charts’ internal reporting workflow to flag it for review.

